  "result": "Excellent! All 113 tests pass. Here's a summary of the VAT implementation:\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **lineVat() function**: Calculates VAT per line on the amount after discount\n   - Formula: (line total - discount) \u00d7 vatRate / 100\n   - Results are rounded per line\n\n2. **invoiceTotals() enhancement**:\n   - Now returns `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`\n   - VAT is the sum of all rounded line VATs\n   - total = subtotal - discount + vat\n   - All values clamped at 0\n\n3. **renderInvoiceText() enhancement**:\n   - Displays VAT line above total (only if VAT > 0)\n   - Format: \"VAT: \u20acX.XX\" before \"Total: \u20acX.XX\"\n   - Output now includes: number/DRAFT, customer name, line items, VAT (if any), total\n\n4. **Comprehensive test coverage (113 total, all passing)**:\n   - lineVat calculation tests (with and without discounts, various VAT rates)\n   - invoiceTotals tests with VAT (single/multiple lines, mixed rates)\n   - VAT with discount combinations\n   - Updated all existing tests to include VAT calculations\n   - Updated render tests to expect VAT in output\n\n**Key design decisions:**\n- VAT is always computed per line, rounded per line, then summed for invoice total (never a percentage of the invoice total)\n- VAT applies to the amount after discount: (qty \u00d7 unitPrice - discount) \u00d7 vatRate / 100\n- VAT line only displays in rendered output if VAT > 0",
